-- title:
--   Toric quotient of the finite part over the decomposition ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a modulus $M$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit that becomes $1$ under the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$, and a valuation subring $Pl$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $Pl$ (the predicate `LiesOverPrime`) whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$. Write $R_D$ for the subring $Pl \cap \mathrm{Fix}(D)$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, where $D =$ `Pl.decompositionSubgroup ℚ`, and assume $R_D$ is a discrete valuation ring. Write $R(p)$ for the subring of $\mathbb{Q}$ of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$, and $J_H(M) = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the geometric function field of $X_H(M)$.
--
--   The curve side consists of: the hypothesis `hj` that the $q$-expansion `jqModC ℚ` of $j$ lies in the $q$-expansion function field at level $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$; a two-chart integral model package $\mathfrak{X}$ of type `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` over $R(p)$ (properness, flatness, integrality, normality and finite presentation for the level-$\Gamma_M$ model, properness and smoothness of relative dimension $1$ for the level-$\Gamma_N$ model, together with an identification of the geometric fibre with a curve model of the function field of $X_H(M)$ compatible with Galois action and with $q$-expansions, summarised here); level data $\Lambda$ of type `JHNeronObjectAtP.LevelData p M H hpM Pl`; and a Néron object $O$ of type `JHNeronObjectAtP p M H hpM Pl hPl Λ`, that is a smooth separated group scheme $O.G \to$ `base p` with relative group law $O.L$, a dictionary $O.\mathrm{pts}$ between $J_H(M)$ and generic sections, Hecke operators and the further axioms of that structure, among them its toric rank $O.\mathrm{toricRank}$.
--
--   The representability hypotheses `hrep` and `hrepΛ` assert that the sub-Picard condition `algEquivZeroCut` (rigidified line bundles whose fibres over algebraically closed points are algebraically equivalent to zero) on the level-$\Gamma_M$ model, rigidified along $\mathfrak{X}.\varepsilon_{\inf}$, is represented by the designation $(O.G, O.g)$ with zero section the unit of $O.L$, and correspondingly that the same condition on the level-$\Gamma_N$ model, rigidified along $\mathfrak{X}.\varepsilon_{\inf}$ followed by $\mathfrak{X}.\pi$, is represented by $(\Lambda.X, \Lambda.f)$ with zero section the unit of $\Lambda.L$.
--
--   The input datum is a $p$-divisible group $\mathcal{G}^D$ over $R_D$ of height $h$, that is a tower of finite free cocommutative Hopf $R_D$-algebras $\mathcal{G}^D.\mathrm{level}\,v$ of rank $p^{vh}$ with surjective transitions whose kernels are the $p^v$-torsion ideals, together with an additive map $\Delta^D$ from the direct limit $\mathcal{G}^D.\mathrm{Points}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to $J_H(M)$ and a realisation of $\mathcal{G}^D$ inside $O.G$. The hypotheses on these data are: `hΔDinj`, injectivity of $\Delta^D$; `hΔDlev`, that for each $v$ the image under $\Delta^D$ of the level-$v$ points is exactly $O.\mathrm{finPts}(p^v)$, the subgroup of $J_H(M)$ generated by the $p^v$-torsion classes whose section extends to the place $\Lambda.\sigma_A$; `hΔDgal`, that $\Delta^D(\tau' \cdot z) = \tau \cdot \Delta^D(z)$ whenever $\tau$ is an automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, $\tau'$ an automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $R_D$, and $\tau'$ agrees with $\tau$ pointwise; `htorD`, that $O.\mathrm{toricPts}(p^v) \le O.\mathrm{finPts}(p^v)$ for all $v$, where $O.\mathrm{toricPts}(m)$ is generated by the range of $O.\mathrm{toricPoint}\,m$; a ring map $\rho^D : R(p) \to R_D$ with `hρD` saying that $\rho^D$ followed by $R_D \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the structure map $R(p) \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; and morphisms $\iota^D_v : \mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal{G}^D.\mathrm{level}\,v) \to O.G$ subject to: `hιDbase`, compatibility of $\iota^D_v$ followed by $O.g$ with the structure maps through $\rho^D$; `hιDcl`, that the resulting map to the base change of $O.G$ along $\mathrm{Spec}\,\rho^D$ is a closed immersion; `hιDp`, that $\iota^D_v$ followed by multiplication by $p^v$ for $O.L$ is the unit section, so the level-$v$ points are killed by $p^v$; `hιDmul`, that for every $v$, every commutative $R_D$-algebra $B$ and all $x, y \in \mathcal{G}^D.\mathrm{Point}\,B\,v$ satisfying the base compatibilities `hx`, `hy`, the section attached to the convolution product $x y$ is the $O.L$-product of the sections attached to $x$ and $y$; `hιDt`, that $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the transition $\mathcal{G}^D.\mathrm{transition}\,v$ followed by $\iota^D_{v+1}$ equals $\iota^D_v$; `hιDfin`, that for each $v$ (given the two compatibility equalities `h3`, `h4`) the canonical morphism $j_v$ from $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal{G}^D.\mathrm{level}\,v)$ into the base change along $\mathrm{Spec}\,\rho^D$ of the $p^v$-torsion pullback in $O.G$ is simultaneously an open and a closed immersion, and every point of that pullback lying over the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,R_D$ is in the image of $j_v$; and `hιDpts`, that for every level-$v$ point $x$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the section $O.\mathrm{pts}$ of the class $\Delta^D(x)$ is $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the algebra map of $x$ followed by $\iota^D_v$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses there exist a $p$-divisible group $\mathcal{T}$ over $R_D$ of height $O.\mathrm{toricRank}$ and, for every $v$, an $R_D$-bialgebra map $\pi_v : \mathcal{G}^D.\mathrm{level}\,v \to \mathcal{T}.\mathrm{level}\,v$ such that:
--
--   (i) every $\pi_v$ is surjective;
--
--   (ii) the tower is compatible: $\mathcal{T}.\mathrm{transition}\,v \circ \pi_{v+1} = \pi_v \circ \mathcal{G}^D.\mathrm{transition}\,v$ for all $v$;
--
--   (iii) for every $v$ and every $x \in \mathcal{G}^D.\mathrm{Point}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})\,v$, the point $x$ factors through $\pi_v$ — that is, there is $y \in \mathcal{T}.\mathrm{Point}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})\,v$ with the algebra map of $y$ precomposed with $\pi_v$ equal to $x$ — if and only if $\Delta^D$ of the class of $x$ lies in $O.\mathrm{toricPts}(p^v)$;
--
--   (iv) every $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of $\mathcal{T}$ reduces to the identity: for all $v$, all $y \in \mathcal{T}.\mathrm{Point}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})\,v$ and all $c \in \mathcal{T}.\mathrm{level}\,v$, the valuation attached to $Pl$ of $y(c) - \varepsilon(c)$ is $< 1$, where $\varepsilon$ is the counit of $\mathcal{T}.\mathrm{level}\,v$ followed by $R_D \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$;
--
--   (v) the toric points are stable under the decomposition group: for every $v$, every automorphism $\tau$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and every automorphism $\tau'$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $R_D$ agreeing with $\tau$ pointwise, $z \in O.\mathrm{toricPts}(p^v)$ implies $\tau \cdot z \in O.\mathrm{toricPts}(p^v)$.
--
--   This is the construction of the toric quotient $p$-divisible group of the finite part of the $p$-power torsion of the Néron object of $J_H(M)$ over the decomposition ring $R_D$ at a place above $p$, in the setting $p \,\|\, M$ where the reduction is multiplicative; conjunct (iv) records that the toric tower is of multiplicative type, and (v) the stability of the toric classes under the decomposition group. It feeds the Raynaud-quotient step [`ModularCurve.exists_pDivisibleGroup_raynaudQuotient_toricPts_and_exists_retraction_finitePart_jHNeronObjectAtP_of_closedImmersion`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_pDivisibleGroup_raynaudQuotient_toricPts_and_exists_retraction_finitePart_jHNeronObjectAtP_of_closedImmersion).
